TASK-132.13 UI runtime harness (AC #5): the sidebar "controlled by an extension"
indicator and the in-window capsule with Stop. Temporary code, never committed
to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task132.13-ui-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .derived build
    open -n -g .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app \
        --env DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify13213UI-<n> --env DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT"
    # Each "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line in $OUT/verify.log is a cue to run
    # `screencapture -x -o -l<windowNumber>`; the harness pauses ~2.5 s after each.
    # Ends with "done". Kill the pid it logs; delete the run's
    # "NSWindow Frame BrowserWindow-<dir>" and "NSSplitView Subview Frames
    # BrowserSplitView-<dir>" defaults keys afterwards.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task132.13-ui-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

It seeds five data: tabs (Delta|Echo a split), registers a "debugger" Stop
handler that detaches, attaches owners "Claude" (Alpha selected, Bravo and Echo
unselected) and "Helper" (Echo), and logs every tab's owners, hosting, capsule
state and frame, the web view frame, each row's indicator and tooltip, and the
page's innerWidth x innerHeight. It shoots light and dark, presses Stop with a
posted NSEvent click (the pointer does not move), selects the parked Bravo,
then the split, and stops the unfocused pane.

